    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0834" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/425: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-29T18:00:00-06:00">December 29,
                            1932—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>119. Amapala retaken by Nationalist troops without opposition after former
                    Commandant fled to Nicaragua last night. Insurgent <pb facs="0835" n="731"
                        xml:id="pg731"/> force mentioned my telegram No. 117, December 27, 1
                        p.m.,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d774-f1"/> marching rapidly toward San Marcos
                    pursued by large force Nationalist troops. Former will probably cross Nicaraguan
                    boundary. Garrison in Tegucigalpa which under control of the Government was
                    source of danger turned over to Nationalist troops and Blue General appointed
                    Commandant Province of Tegucigalpa.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
